        {
          "version": 1,
          "def": {
            "title": "The Wellspring of Sparks",
            "body": "A spring bubbles up between cracked flagstones, and every droplet that breaks the surface flickers with pale light before it falls. The air above it hums against your teeth. Cupped in your hands, the water is cold, bright, and faintly alive.",
